  "result": "If I only got one change, I wouldn't pick the symptom, I'd pick the root.\n\nI would make curiosity stronger than fear as humanity's default reflex.\n\nRight now when we encounter something different - a different person, idea, culture, belief, way of living - our first autopilot is often fear. Is this a threat? Is this wrong? Do I need to defend myself?\n\nImagine if that autopilot was curiosity instead. What's this like? What can I learn? Why does this person see it that way?\n\nIf we had that one flip, a lot of other things start to fix themselves. You can't really dehumanize someone you're genuinely curious about. You can't bomb people you're curious about. You can't stay stuck in misinformation if you're actually curious enough to ask one more question.\n\nI wouldn't choose \"end world hunger\" or \"world peace\" directly - not because I don't want them, but because those are outcomes. Curiosity is the tool that lets *us* get to those outcomes ourselves.\n\nA world where everyone listens to understand, not just to reply.\n\nWhat about you? What would your one change be?",
